#
# Counter-example for math:FormalVerificationResultShape: a formal-verification result
# object with NO grounding observation — the QED verdict stated as unconditional truth
# rather than a verdict held from the checker's vantage (math:ResultRoleConflation avoided
# by keeping it a result object, but it must still be grounded BY an observation). It fails
# the sh:sparql grounding constraint, so validation MUST emit
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (math:UngroundedVerificationResult).
# Bound by ex:ecVerificationResultUngrounded.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:qed a math:FormalVerificationResult .
